tern to me is that the compiler optimizes the dominant constrained cost, not just generic speed. For real-time C, that means reducing a safe upper bound on execution time; for distributed quantum circuits, it means reducing depth and link-generation pressure under scarce network resources.\\\",\n            \\\"parent_ref\\\": \\\"draft-2\\\",\n            \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n                \\\"score\\\": 22,\n                \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Concise and well-grounded in the two source contexts, though it is less detailed than the strongest comments.\\\"\n            }\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\nwith output_path.open('w', encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n    json.dump(payload, handle, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n    handle.write('\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
